    },
    {
      "ordinal": 4,
      "section": "1. Introduction",
      "paragraph_hash": "0606125f705bb47d5da9fdc0811a2e7564a833252a85aba797a4202c7e5cdce3",
      "text_length": 1340,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Nowadays, based on traditional algorithms, much methods has been made in the detection of apple leaf diseases, artificia"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 5,
      "section": "1. Introduction",
      "paragraph_hash": "98662a812ce09e043f825348950b02ca6dd7cf9ed48277d449f6c08280f5c718",
      "text_length": 2314,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Since the emergence of target detection technology during the 1960s, many domestic and overseas investigators have focus"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 6,
      "section": "1. Introduction",
      "paragraph_hash": "ce3aeede84f391a47cb985f84aef0c0e48f8afc344c37f0800490faecb1353cc",
      "text_length": 2046,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Convolutional neural network learning methods are now being applied to classify and identify apple leaf diseases, such a"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 7,
      "section": "1. Introduction",
      "paragraph_hash": "643521cecf3fa21a7a45ff9e44a9250118eebea758390524d936c39f90f3ff9e",
      "text_length": 1757,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "There are two main types of target detection in the deep learning era [33]. The first is based on region formation. Repr"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 8,
      "section": "2.1.1 YOLO network model",
      "paragraph_hash": "2e397d8997adc9d4f4fbde2e5f6f42d60ace771523c915f49bc86d5aaea01c5b",
      "text_length": 752,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "The core principle of YOLO is the consideration that target detection is a regression problem. In this algorithm, images"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 9,
      "section": "2.1.1 YOLO network model",
      "paragraph_hash": "ef14c630769ab2fd1f20b7fb2f11e5f8699372539bc0d998669091ffdc755701",
      "text_length": 646,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "In Eq (1), Pr(object) is the probability that a target object falls into the grid, which is a standard for measuring the"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 10,
      "section": "2.1.1 YOLO network model",
      "paragraph_hash": "5aab8a666d32a5ee54472a7c20203ac5220aadb1c3d27ff59115283435a0587f",
      "text_length": 458,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "On this basis, YOLO selects the appropriate candidate region to predict while detecting the input picture to obtain the "
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 11,
      "section": "2.1.2 YOLOv2 network",
      "paragraph_hash": "5a396cbc9042fef4a80cc6230cb1fc2d95962a004a503e971b9d48ca1e1ba9dd",
      "text_length": 1453,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Although YOLO has been greatly improved in terms of detection speed, its detection accuracy is far from optimal. Object "
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 12,
      "section": "2.1.3 Tiny-YOLO network",
      "paragraph_hash": "0e723d63f639cc9293e5a15382c34652490ffc792698d614ff5b27c3e7bc4269",
      "text_length": 614,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Tiny-YOLO is a miniature “accelerated version” network based on the Darknet-19 structure (Fig 1). This reduces the compl"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 13,
      "section": "2.1.3 Tiny-YOLO network",
      "paragraph_hash": "b7788b547d84b1804a381adec43d3d83a5ba51ef00e601c757a6dbd1cfe3c552",
      "text_length": 60,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Tiny-YOLO structure and the network parameter shown in here."
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 14,
      "section": "2.1.4 Dense connective network",
      "paragraph_hash": "789415cbb158f60842454bdfc4e18fa38deb24e7107271b3959235f0392b6681",
      "text_length": 323,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Huang, Liu [40] connected all layers in the network in pairs so that each layer in the network can receive the character"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 15,
      "section": "2.1.4 Dense connective network",
      "paragraph_hash": "965c9e135f8962a5e8de559079deb6988bc812fd42b5f2a77539a835520fb71d",
      "text_length": 1059,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "DenseNet has the following important characteristics. It alleviates the problem of gradient dissipation during training "
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 16,
      "section": "2.1.4 Dense connective network",
      "paragraph_hash": "4323792b65ce156229e2fed8e65e66ec44f86192b4e30d4a1ec29d31a3d54a4c",
      "text_length": 253,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "DenseNet encourages feature reuse, which means that the features of each picture can be used, and this reduces disappear"
    },
    {
      "ordinal": 17,
      "section": "2.1.5 F-YOLO network",
      "paragraph_hash": "819237591802e23172b98bf14e7286ff9ebeda5eb7dd591398b081d54d816b6d",
      "text_length": 1027,
      "native_jats_id": null,
      "preview": "Mehta and Ozturk [41] proposed F-YOLO based on Tiny-YOLO. Generally, a deeper and wider network structure, results in a "
    },
    {
